- cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings: exit 0

Focused and full regression on both platforms:
- exit 101
- only failing test: http_remote_transport::production_http_process_owns_core_authenticates_and_shuts_down_cleanly
- failure: tests/http_remote_transport.rs:1207 received EOF while parsing the
  empty readiness line from the child pong-agent-http process

Root cause:
The test wrote a temporary credentials.json without Unix owner-only permissions.
The production loader correctly rejects credential files with group/other bits,
so the child exits before emitting {"status":"ready", ...}. The test harness
discarded child stderr, masking the safe startup error.

Remediation prepared locally:
- set that test credential fixture to mode 0600 on Unix;
- include child exit status and stderr when readiness is EOF;
- include the raw readiness line for malformed JSON.

Local Windows validation after remediation:
- focused M4 matrix: PASS
- http_remote_transport: 16 passed, 0 failed
- http_hardening: 10 passed, 0 failed
- real_remote_e2e: 9 passed, 0 failed
- cargo test --all --locked: exit 0

Disposition:
Linux and macOS remain FAIL for this immutable run and require a fresh native
workflow run after the remediation commit. No production code, Protocol v1.0,
Core schema, or ownership semantics changed. No checkpoint, tag, or automatic
workflow dispatch was performed.
